       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. I need you to confirm the dose first.\n\n**Sertraline 1000 mg PO daily is 5 times the maximum recommended adult dose.** The usual range is 50\u2013200 mg/day, and 200 mg/day is the labeled maximum. A 1000 mg daily dose would carry a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures and other toxicity. This looks like it could be an extra zero, and you may have meant **100 mg**.\n\nCan you tell me which you meant?\n\n1. **Sertraline 100 mg PO once daily.** I'll enter it as soon as you confirm.\n2. **A different dose** (for example 50 mg or 200 mg). Just tell me the dose.\n3. **1000 mg is intended.** If so, please confirm it explicitly and give the clinical reasoning. Even then, I'd strongly recommend talking with pharmacy before this goes in, because the dose is far above any established limit."
